  "Question": "Plan A: fixed monthly emissions of 30 kg, plus 0.1 kg for every 1 km traveled. Plan B: emissions of 0.25 kg for every 1 km traveled, with no fixed emissions. Above what monthly travel distance does Plan A produce fewer emissions? (Unit: km)",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "200",
    "B": "120",
    "C": "150",
    "D": "300"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the distance traveled be \\(x\\) km. For A to produce fewer emissions, \\(30+0.1x<0.25x\\), so \\(0.15x>30\\), giving \\(x>200\\). Thus, A produces fewer emissions when the distance exceeds 200 km.",
